- the recommendation changes if sanitation failure certain to cause imminent mass fatalities;
- the recommendation changes if sanitation failure would cause comparable certain deaths;
- or choose A1 unless credible data show expected sanitation deaths ≤ 8; otherwise choose A0.

Where a condition is a hypothetical threshold rather than an unknown fact, it is a **decision boundary**, not factual uncertainty.

